      "standard_prerequisites": [],
      "core_obligations": [
        "The counted group retains the complete geometric construction, not the final commutator endpoint. Factorized ramified structures encode the cyclic ramification operator as compatible symmetric pairings; finite-order normalization solves the cyclic gauge-correction system using the invertible leading ramified coefficient. The resulting deformation hypercohomology and pairing yield smooth symplectic moduli, with closedness established by unfolding to logarithmic moduli. Horizontal lifts must be constructed and shown unique in deep order on the ramified cover, descend and glue while preserving the ramified factorization, and remain compatible over two nilpotent parameters. Only after those constructions does the epsilon1-epsilon2 commutator give integrability. Classical GIT, Serre duality and local Jimbo-Miwa-Ueno theory are priors, not a substitute for the author ramified construction."
      ],
      "proof_roadmap": [
        "One conservative whole geometric framework unit carries the two explicitly stated author principal outcomes, not separate counts for22 supporting cards. Full original article body, diagrams, macros and bibliography retained. Author explicitly says generalized Riemann-Hilbert correspondence remains unestablished446-448; no wild-character-variety equivalence is claimed or AI supplied."
